# Shopmine Automation Implementation Plan

This plan outlines the creation of a Python script to automatically run the "Shopmine" program at a specific time daily. It also includes a guide for an alternative method using Windows Task Scheduler.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Executable Path**: The script will require the absolute path to the Shopmine executable (`.exe`). I will use a placeholder path in the code which you will need to update, or I can add logic to prompt for it.
> **Python Environment**: The script requires Python and the `schedule` library. I will include instructions for setting this up.

## Proposed Changes

### `c:\Upload2601공유폴더\샵마인 자동화`

#### [NEW] [run_shopmine.py](file:///c:/Upload2601공유폴더/샵마인%20자동화/run_shopmine.py)
- A Python script that:
    - Imports `schedule`, `time`, `subprocess`, `os`.
    - Defines a configuration section for `SHOPMINE_PATH` and `SCHEDULE_TIME`.
    - Defines a function `run_job()` to launch the program.
    - Sets up the schedule loop.
    - Includes error handling (e.g., if path is incorrect).

#### [NEW] [README.md](file:///c:/Upload2601공유폴더/샵마인%20자동화/README.md)
- Documentation on:
    - How to install Python and dependencies (`pip install schedule`).
    - How to configure the script (path and time).
    - How to run the script.
    - **Alternative**: Step-by-step guide to using Windows Task Scheduler for the same purpose (often more reliable for system tasks).

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- I will create a dummy "Shopmine" script (e.g., a simple python script that prints "Shopmine started") to test the scheduling logic without launching the actual heavy program.
- Run `run_shopmine.py` with the dummy script path and a time 1 minute from now to verify it triggers.

### Manual Verification
- User to update the `SHOPMINE_PATH` to the real executable.
- User to run the script and verify Shopmine opens at the scheduled time.
